.TH WREX-DHCP6 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-dhcp6 \- dhcp6 layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIdhcp6\fR \fB--dhcp6\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIdhcp6\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
DHCPv6 (RFC 8415) over UDP 546/547: the 4\-byte fixed header (msg_type 1\-13 + the 3\-byte trans_id) — everything else is options (u16 code, u16 len TLVs; the options grammar with nested sub\-options is the recorded tranche\-17c tail). udp dispatches ports 546/547 into this codec.
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 40; stacks on udp (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --dhcp6-msg_type).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp6\-msg_type=\fIINT\fR\fR
message type (1 solicit, 2 advertise, 3 request, 4 reply, 5 release, 6 decline, 8 info_req, 9 renew, 10 rebind, 12 relay_forward, 13 relay_reply; raw numbers kept) Type u8. Default: 1.
.TP
\fB\-\-dhcp6\-trans_id=\fIINT\fR\fR
transaction id (3 bytes on the wire; over\-wide values mask) Type u32. Default: 0.

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex fields dhcp6

